module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.surface_shorthand_preempts_resolved_identity

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { NoRungStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data surface_shorthand_preempts_resolved_identity: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "surface_shorthand_preempts_resolved_identity" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: NoRungStated },

  receipts: [
    "**surface shorthand preempts resolved identity** (a semantic consumer dispatches on a raw lexeme after resolution has already named its declaration, so a declared constructor is reinterpreted as a host sentinel or primitive.",

    "Recognition rule: once a node carries a binding/declaration identity, value construction must be total over that identity; spelling may be interpreted only on an explicitly unresolved shorthand arm.",

    "Specimen gunbc#9741: bare and imported `None` became host `Null` while qualified `Diagnostics.None {}` became a `Variant`; a single-frame comparison hid the fork.",

    "This is not hollow alias: the binding is grounded and present, then discarded downstream.",

    "It is also separate from the per-frame symbol-ordinal defect: that defect corrupted lexeme identity while crossing frames, whereas this one ignores an identity already supplied at one construction site.",

    "SECOND SPECIMEN (2026-09-11, v1_interpreter eval_var's variable slow path, gunbc#11065). The evaluator held the resolved node from the file-aware resolver and still took the item KIND from item_registry, a projection keyed by bare SPELLING that keeps one homonym per spelling in hash-seed order. One fact, two authorities: a data reference to extdeps.vendor.gigabyte's gigabyte was classified by std.measure's fn gigabyte on some processes and evaluated as a function, and a field read refused with cannot access field 'legal_name' on Fn. Found at: mitigatable where the wrong kind reached a typed refusal, and silent wrongness wherever a mis-kinded value flows on without one. The instrument that exposed and discharges it is an N-run comparison across per-process hash seeds on one probe, a control binary built from the base against the repaired binary, recorded on gunbc#11065; test.claim.data_reference_kind_from_resolved_node is only a probabilistic regression control for it, never its coverage.",

    "WHAT THAT REPAIR CLOSES AND WHAT IT LEAVES, per path, because the rung is the minimum across them -- enumerated over every item_registry read in v1_interpreter. CLOSED: eval_var now takes the kind from item_kind of the resolved node, the function that computed the registry's kind, so its kind and node can no longer disagree. KIND COLLAPSED, SELECTION NOT: eval_data_item_value, eval_data_initializer_values and resolve_published_mock_keys classify the node they evaluate (resolve_published_mock_keys for UNIFORMITY, not to fix a live instance: on main no data declaration typed PublishedMockCase shares its name with any other data, fn, type, service or resource declaration, so that site is not reachable by the data/fn homonym today; a same-spelled COPRODUCT ARM was NOT checked, and that channel -- an arm is not a local binding under its own spelling, so it lands in the pool -- is exactly the one binding_chosen_by_pool_membership_rather_than_by_the_declared_rule is about, so this is unchecked there, not clear), but they are asked by bare name with no referring file and still SELECT that node through the shared bare slot, whose owner for a colliding spelling is chosen by walk order rather than by declaration, so they can still evaluate or decline the wrong declaration. GUARDED: build_initial_env still reads the registry kind but skips every name with more than one declaration, so its registry entry and slot are one declaration. SAME LAW, DIFFERENT MECHANISM, LEFT OPEN: try_witness_evaluation_dispatch and the two v2 collection grounding gates hold a resolved node yet ask the bare registry which MODULE it belongs to, so a homonym can attribute the node to another module and misroute a primitive dispatch; closing them needs node-to-module attribution, not item_kind. OUT OF CLASS: resolution_fingerprint observes the projection itself rather than reading what a name denotes. The class therefore stays mitigatable on every path but eval_var.",

    "NEXT RUNG FOR THIS SPECIMEN, a capability and not an artifact: an ambiguous bare name that reaches the shared slot is REFUSED, landed together with the renames that make the corpus pass it and never with an allow-list, so a reference with no declaration-aware answer has no evaluation at all. That makes the ambiguity unwritable rather than unlikely to be observed, and it is the step the existing trigger below names for evaluator construction in general.",

    "THIRD SPECIMEN (2026-09-19, gunbc#11603, review 68098/68166). A bare `Https` or `Http`, imported by name from extdeps.uri, evaluates to NoSuchVariable in any closure that also reaches gunbc.cloudflare.r2_origin, while the same literal evaluates in a minimal module; v2.extdeps.coordination CoordinationEffectKind also declares an `Http` variant, and the resolved import is discarded for a bare-spelling lookup that the colliding family defeats. The module-qualified `extdeps.uri.Https` evaluates correctly in the same closure, which is the discriminator and the route #11603 now uses (the interim uri_scheme_is_https predicate was deleted). Still open: the bare imported form. Reproduce with `gunbc run --entry dag/test/claim/cloudflare_boot_origin_witness.dag --function readback_refuses_plain_http` after replacing the qualified reference in boot_origin.dag with the bare imported one.",

    "FOURTH SPECIMEN (2026-09-24, gunbc#12185, found by side-chat review). The service-receiver stamp joins on the bare NAME, not the owning declaration: v1.compiler.infer infer_var_binding_kind stamps ServiceValueBinding when the service registry holds the local's name and the local's type is the nominal reference the scope fold inserted (local_is_service_root_binding), without comparing that reference's owner module to the registry row's. gunbc.runner.runner_guest_image calls `Filesystem.Write(...)` and reads `.success`/`.error`, which is extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io's service Filesystem. When #12185 first named a source for that bare read, it imported std.resources { Filesystem } (a resource whose capability is lowercase `write` with output `written`), and the module still type-checked and emitted, because the registry row matched by name. The import was corrected to extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io { Filesystem }, checked by reading the call: `.success` and `.error` exist only on that service's Write, not on the resource's `write`. The join itself is unrepaired. THE DISCRIMINATING RED IS UNAUTHORABLE ON EVERY ROUTE TODAY: on the seed, the name-only join is the defect, so a mutant import back to std.resources type-checks and emits green; on v2, v2.extdeps.languages.dag has no resource production (the resource shape refuses at parse) and v2.compiler.namespace_graft places only fn/data/type declarations in the containment tree, so a service receiver has no declaring path to assert. Next rung, two capabilities, either of which makes the red authorable: (a) the seed's service stamp requires the local's resolved declaration and the registry row to be the SAME declaration (owner module plus name), so a two-declaration fixture refuses the mutant import at the call; (b) v2 grafts service declarations into the containment tree and gains a resource production, so the receiver's declaring path is assertable.",

    "FIFTH SPECIMEN (2026-11-01, v1.compiler.emit_rust effective_variant_parent, follow-up to gunbc#15565). The emitter held the binding kind inference had already stamped on the node and still took the variant PARENT from emit_info.variant_to_enum, a closure-wide projection keyed by the bare arm SPELLING that v1.compiler.emit_info derive_variant_to_enum folds from every coproduct in the closure. A parameter or `let` written with an arm's AUTHORED spelling was rendered as the arm: beside `type ShadowColor = Red { rank: Int } | Green { rank: Int }`, `fn control_arm_shadow_param(Red: Int) -> Int { Red + 1 }` emitted `ShadowColor::Red` in an Int position, so the emitted crate does not build. A wrong construction, not a stray import -- and the second spelling rule in the same function fails the same way: effective_variant_parent_from_resolved calls is_optional_variant_name and elects the parent `Optional` for any optional-cardinality value whose name is spelled `Present`, `Absent`, `Some` or `None`. Both were reachable because a spelling was read first; the fact that answers them, the binding kind, was already in the node's hand. Same class as the SECOND SPECIMEN one link along: there the evaluator held the resolved node and took the KIND from item_registry, here the emitter holds the resolved binding kind and takes the parent from a flat map. Found at: the #15565 follow-up census of the bare-name reads that outlived that PR, walked from the EmitGraphInfo field list rather than grepped (v1 04_* / 05_emit_rust and src/v2/compiler); #15565 had gated the sibling read in lookup_item_for_value_ref and this one was missed by grep alone.",
    "RUNG FOR THE FIFTH SPECIMEN: effective_variant_parent returns none for LocalValueBinding and MatchBoundBinding before either the flat map or the resolved-type membership test -- the authority #15565 installed beside it in the same file, so the emitter's two remaining bare-name registry reads now agree. Control: dag/gunbc/instruments/native_emission_controls `local_binder_shadows_coproduct_arm_cases`, param and let rows red before (the emitted program named the arm where the local was meant) and held after, plus a third row holding the other side of the gate, that a GENUINE arm reference still elects its parent.",
    "CEILING ON THE FIFTH SPECIMEN, stated rather than closed: of the two kinds the gate names, only LocalValueBinding has a colliding form the native route can build. A match-bound binder cannot carry the needed spelling -- v1 reads an uppercase PATTERN atom as a VARIANT, so a `ControlRedBox { red: Red }` binder is refused as `missing required field 'rank' in literal of type 'Red'` rather than binding a variable -- and a snake_case field binder could only collide with a lowercase arm, which is itself unbuildable: a variant is emitted verbatim and neither `non_camel_case_types` nor `non_snake_case` is in v1.compiler.emit_rust generated_rust_lint_relaxations, so the native route's `-D warnings` build refuses a lowercase arm outright. That is also why the corpus never met this: binders are emitted with their first letter lower-cased while variants are emitted verbatim, so the two namespaces can only meet in authored text. The flat map therefore stays keyed by bare spelling for everything that can still reach it, and a second consumer of variant_to_enum able to see a value occurrence reopens this row.",
    "Next-rung trigger: host literals and intentional primitive representations are typed parser/resolver constructions, and evaluator value construction is total over every resolved binding with no raw-spelling arm able to override it.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
